[C,docs/instructions.md,52] Next, you can set some options.
[C,docs/instructions.md,53] 
[C,docs/instructions.md,54] 
[C,docs/instructions.md,55] ## Setting Options
[C,docs/instructions.md,56] 
[C,docs/instructions.md,57] There are default options you can set before, or when you create a new client.
[C,docs/instructions.md,58] 
[C,docs/instructions.md,59] ```js
[C,docs/instructions.md,60] var _defaults = {
[C,docs/instructions.md,61]   moviePath:         "ZeroClipboard.swf",        // URL to movie
[D,docs/instructions.md,62]   trustedDomains:    undefined,                  // Domains that we should trust (single string or array of strings)
[A,docs/instructions.md,62]   trustedOrigins:    null,                       // Page origins that the SWF should trust (single string or array of strings)
[C,docs/instructions.md,63]   hoverClass:        "zeroclipboard-is-hover",   // The class used to hover over the object
[C,docs/instructions.md,64]   activeClass:       "zeroclipboard-is-active",  // The class used to set object active
[C,docs/instructions.md,65]   allowScriptAccess: "sameDomain",               // SWF outbound scripting policy
[C,docs/instructions.md,66]   useNoCache:        true,                       // Include a nocache query parameter on requests for the SWF
[C,docs/instructions.md,67]   forceHandCursor:   false                       // Forcibly set the hand cursor ("pointer") for all glued elements
[C,docs/instructions.md,68] };
[C,docs/instructions.md,69] ```
[C,docs/instructions.md,70] You can override the defaults using `ZeroClipboard.setDefaults({ moviePath: "new/path" })` before you create any clients.
[C,docs/instructions.md,71] 
[C,docs/instructions.md,72] You can also set the options when creating a new client by passing an optional json object `new ZeroClipboard($("#d_clip_button"), { moviePath: "new/path", text: "Copy me!" })`
[C,docs/instructions.md,73] 
[C,docs/instructions.md,74] 
[A,docs/instructions.md,75] ### A note on the `trustedOrigins` option
[A,docs/instructions.md,76] 
[A,docs/instructions.md,77] If your ZeroClipboard SWF is served from a different origin/domain than your page, you need to tell the SWF that it's OK to trust your page. The following is almost _**always**_ how you want to do this:
[A,docs/instructions.md,78] 
[A,docs/instructions.md,79] ```js
[A,docs/instructions.md,80] ZeroClipboard.setDefaults({
[A,docs/instructions.md,81]   trustedOrigins: [window.location.protocol + "//" + window.location.host]
[A,docs/instructions.md,82] });
[A,docs/instructions.md,83] ```
[A,docs/instructions.md,84] 
[A,docs/instructions.md,85] 
[C,docs/instructions.md,86] ### A note on the `allowScriptAccess` option
[C,docs/instructions.md,87] 
[C,docs/instructions.md,88] For version 1.1.7 and below, the `embed` tag had the `allowScriptAccess` parameter hard-coded to `always`. This allowed the "`ZeroClipboard.swf`" file to be hosted on an external domain. However, to enhance security, versions after 1.1.7 have an option for `allowScriptAccess` with a default of `sameDomain`, which only allows "`ZeroClipboard.swf`" to be served from the same domain as the hosting page.
[C,docs/instructions.md,89] 
[C,docs/instructions.md,90] If you hosted "`ZeroClipboard.swf`" on a different domain than the hosting page on version 1.1.7 or below, when you upgrade to a version above 1.1.7, you should either move "`ZeroClipboard.swf`" to the same domain as the hosting page or set the `allowScriptAccess` option to `always`.
[C,docs/instructions.md,91] 
[C,docs/instructions.md,92] For more information about `allowScriptAccess`, consult the *[official Flash documentation](http://helpx.adobe.com/flash/kb/control-access-scripts-host-web.html)*.
[C,docs/instructions.md,93] 
[C,docs/instructions.md,94] 
[C,docs/instructions.md,95] ### Cross-Protocol Limitations
[C,docs/instructions.md,96] 
[C,docs/instructions.md,97] ZeroClipboard was intentionally configured to _not_ allow the SWF to be served from a secure domain (HTTPS) but scripted by an insecure domain (HTTP).
[C,docs/instructions.md,98] 
[C,docs/instructions.md,99] If you find yourself in this situation (as in [Issue #170](https://github.com/zeroclipboard/ZeroClipboard/issues/170)), please consider the following options:  
[C,docs/instructions.md,100]  1. Serve the SWF over HTTP instead of HTTPS. If the page's protocol can vary (e.g. authorized/unauthorized, staging/production, etc.), you should include add the SWF with a relative protocol (`//s3.amazonaws.com/blah/ZeroClipboard.swf`) instead of an absolute protocol (`https://s3.amazonaws.com/blah/ZeroClipboard.swf`).
